        <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> / <a href="rwanda.html">Rwanda</a> / Kigali, Culture &amp; Kivu</nav>
        <p class="article__lead">A gentle, culture-rich Rwanda for families — the creative buzz of Kigali, playful golden monkeys in the Virunga foothills, and lakeside days swimming and sailing on Lake Kivu. Short drives, warm welcomes and plenty for curious young minds.</p>
        <p>Rwanda is clean, safe and exceptionally welcoming, which makes it a wonderful introduction to Africa for children. (Gorilla trekking has a minimum age of 15, so this journey keeps younger travellers happily occupied elsewhere.)</p>
